WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.218
Modelfiles help turn model setup into repeatable operational configuration.

00:00:03.218 --> 00:00:05.643
Instead of relying on undocumented manual choices,

00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:09.800
a Modelfile can describe a base model and the settings that shape

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.878
how an internal model variant behaves.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.650
That may include parameters, templates, system messages, adapters,

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.153
and licensing or source notes that help operators understand what they are running.

00:00:19.153 --> 00:00:23.657
Controlled variants are useful because different teams and workflows often need different defaults.

00:00:23.657 --> 00:00:27.121
A support workflow may need a different tone, context window,

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:30.932
or response style than a developer assistant or a lab experiment.

00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:31.971
Without documented variants,

00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:36.128
teams can end up with several machines that appear to run the

00:00:36.128 --> 00:00:39.592
same model but behave differently because someone changed a prompt,

00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:41.324
template, or runtime option locally.

00:00:41.324 --> 00:00:44.788
System messages and templates should be treated as operational configuration.

00:00:44.788 --> 00:00:48.946
They can affect user experience, safety expectations, support outcomes, and evaluation results.

00:00:48.946 --> 00:00:53.795
When those settings are used for shared workflows, they should be named, reviewed, versioned,

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:54.488
and documented.

00:00:54.488 --> 00:00:58.645
A short note about why a setting exists can prevent confusion later.

00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:02.110
Repeatable configuration reduces drift between developer machines and shared environments.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.842
It also makes troubleshooting easier.

00:01:03.842 --> 00:01:05.574
If a model variant changed,

00:01:05.574 --> 00:01:11.117
teams can compare the Modelfile and related notes rather than guessing which manual step was different.

00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:15.620
This is the difference between local experimentation and a supportable local AI service.
